// Title: Use of OpenConsole
// Sigma ID: 814c95cc-8192-4378-a70a-f1aafd877af1
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects usage of OpenConsole binary as a LOLBIN to launch other binaries to bypass application
//   Whitelisting
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use by an administrator
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/nas_bench/status/1537563834478645252
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_openconsole.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "OpenConsole.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\OpenConsole.exe") and (not(FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\Microsoft.WindowsTerminal"))
